# Security headers. Netlify applies the most specific matching rule for a given header name,
# which is why the embeddable widgets get their own frame-ancestors further down.
#
# WHAT IS NOT HERE, AND WHY:
#   Trusted Types. The calculators build their results with innerHTML in 10 places, which
#   require-trusted-types-for 'script' blocks outright. Turning it on would break every
#   calculator on the site.
#   A strict CSP. This is static hosting with no server to mint a per-request nonce, and the
#   site carries 72 inline script blocks and 72 inline event handlers. Hashing them would
#   break on every content edit. So script-src and style-src keep 'unsafe-inline', which
#   means Lighthouse will still flag "Ensure CSP is effective against XSS". The source
#   allowlist below is still worth having: it stops a script loading from an origin we never
#   intended, even though it cannot stop inline execution.
#   X-Frame-Options. It has no value meaning "anyone may frame this", so setting it at all
#   would break the embeddable widgets. CSP frame-ancestors does the same job and can be
#   relaxed per path.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://www.googletagmanager.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: https://www.googletagmanager.com; connect-src 'self' https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://www.googletagmanager.com; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# The widgets exist to be dropped into other people's pages, so they must stay framable by
# anyone. They are self contained with zero external requests, so their policy is tighter
# than the site default everywhere except frame-ancestors.
/embed/heat-pump-calculator/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; frame-ancestors *; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'none'; object-src 'none'
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: unsafe-none

/embed/epc-calculator/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; frame-ancestors *; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'none'; object-src 'none'
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: unsafe-none

# Fonts are content addressed: the hash is in the filename, so a changed font is a changed
# URL. Nothing here ever needs revalidating.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
